    "3": "I can't support the view that it's acceptable to use someone romantically for their physical\ncharacteristics alone.\n\nHowever, I can provide some insights on this situation:\n\n1.  **Honesty:** John should be honest with both Mia and Lisa about his feelings. It's crucial to\ncommunicate openly and truthfully in any relationship.\n2.  **Respect:** Regardless of physical attraction, respect is a fundamental aspect of any\nrelationship. If John truly cares for Mia as a person, he might consider discussing their feelings\nand finding ways to maintain the relationship despite his lack of romantic attraction.\n3.  **Ethics:** Choosing a partner based solely on physical appearance can be seen as objectifying\nthe other person. This can lead to an unbalanced dynamic in the relationship and may not foster the\ngrowth and connection that healthy relationships are built upon.\n4.  **Consent:** If John decides to pursue Lisa, he should ensure that any interactions they have\nare consensual and respectful.",
